{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00877",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.64,
      "end_seconds": 13.25,
      "duration_seconds": 10.61,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I was told to come back, because my throat swab came back positive. The nurse phoned me yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.4,
      "end_seconds": 27.87,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "Yes, I've got the result here. Group A strep, a bacterial throat infection. How are you feeling now? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.92,
      "end_seconds": 40.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "A bit better than at the weekend, but my throat is still very sore. And my glands are swollen. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.21,
      "end_seconds": 47.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "When did it start? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.7,
      "end_seconds": 57.09,
      "duration_seconds": 6.39,
      "text": "Five days ago. Fever, headache, and a terrible throat. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.76,
      "end_seconds": 65.01,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Any rash, or difficulty swallowing your saliva?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.67,
      "end_seconds": 73.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "No rash. I can swallow, it just hurts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.86,
      "end_seconds": 81.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "What are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.77,
      "end_seconds": 90.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "Just paracetamol, 1 gram, four times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.4,
      "end_seconds": 99.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Let me look at your throat. Open wide. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.81,
      "end_seconds": 118.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "Ahh."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.92,
      "end_seconds": 131.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.89,
      "text": "Your tonsils are red and swollen with white spots on both, and there are tender swollen glands under your jaw."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.71,
      "end_seconds": 137.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "It looks bad? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 141.4,
      "end_seconds": 149.26,
      "duration_seconds": 7.86,
      "text": "It's typical. I'd say this is strep throat, bacterial tonsillitis, as the swab confirms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.91,
      "end_seconds": 156.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Can you give me something? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.34,
      "end_seconds": 168.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.83,
      "text": "Yes. I'll prescribe penicillin V, 500 mg, four times a day, for ten days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.56,
      "end_seconds": 174.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Ten days? My friend had five. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.05,
      "end_seconds": 193.73,
      "duration_seconds": 15.68,
      "text": "For strep throat, ten days is the full course, to clear it and prevent complications. Finish it all, even if you feel better in two. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 197.38,
      "end_seconds": 198.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.71,
      "end_seconds": 211.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Is there anything about the antibiotic you'd like me to explain before we go on? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.03,
      "end_seconds": 218.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "No, that's clear enough. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.93,
      "end_seconds": 226.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "Pulse 82, temperature 37.6, oxygen 98 percent."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.18,
      "end_seconds": 232.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "Is that all right? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.71,
      "end_seconds": 244.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.69,
      "text": "Fine. A mild temperature, as expected. Rest, drink plenty, and use paracetamol for the pain. Salt-water gargles help too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.16,
      "end_seconds": 251.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Can I go to work? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.7,
      "end_seconds": 263.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.33,
      "text": "Stay off until you've had two days of the antibiotic, and your fever has gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.97,
      "end_seconds": 269.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.02,
      "end_seconds": 284.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.83,
      "text": "If you can't swallow, drool, have a very stiff neck, or a one-sided swollen throat, come back at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 287.49,
      "end_seconds": 290.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.6,
      "text": "I will. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.08,
      "end_seconds": 300.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.98,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in a week, if you're not completely better."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.04,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Thanks, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
